753	 * Reveal a hosting database's stored password (owner or admin, never while
754	 * impersonating — same discipline as revealHostingSftpPassword, audit LOW-1). The
755	 * password is kept encrypted on the row now (the provisioner no longer wipes it),
756	 * so a customer can look it up any time. If it was never stored (a legacy row, or a
757	 * WordPress/app DB from before this shipped), they can Reset to set a fresh one.
